**Why `@dataclass`?**
Python `dataclass` auto-generates `__init__`, `__repr__`, and `__eq__` from the field annotations. These are simple data containers — no business logic. `@dataclass` is cleaner than a plain `dict` (typed, auto-documented) and lighter than a `pydantic.BaseModel` (no validation needed here since data comes from a trusted API response).

