### Role: Dependency Specification — Reproducible Environments

```text
osmnx>=1.9.0           # OSM vector ingestion via Overpass API
geopandas>=0.14.0      # GeoDataFrame + CRS transformation
shapely>=2.0.0         # Computational geometry (make_valid, Polygon.area, etc.)
pyproj>=3.6.0          # CRS database + pyproj.Transformer
pyogrio>=0.7.0         # Fast GDAL OGR I/O backend for geopandas

rasterio>=1.3.8        # Raster I/O + warp + COG writing
affine>=2.4.0,<3.0.0   # Affine transform math (dependency of rasterio)
numpy>=1.24.0,<2.0.0   # N-dimensional arrays for pixel data

pystac-client>=0.7.2   # STAC API client (search, filter, paginate)
planetary-computer>=1.0.0  # SAS URL signer for Microsoft PC
requests>=2.31.0       # HTTP client (used by pystac-client)

tenacity>=8.2.3        # Retry with exponential backoff + logging hooks
pyyaml>=6.0.1          # YAML config parser (safe_load)
python-dotenv>=1.0.0   # .env file loader
pydantic>=2.5.0        # Config schema validation
rich>=13.7.0           # (Optional) rich terminal output
tqdm>=4.66.0           # (Optional) progress bars
```

**Version constraints explained:**
- `shapely>=2.0.0` — Shapely 2.x rewrote the C bindings, dramatically improving performance and adding `make_valid()`. Shapely 1.x would break `make_valid()` calls.
- `numpy>=1.24.0,<2.0.0` — NumPy 2.0 introduced breaking API changes (`np.bool`, `np.int` were removed). Pinning below 2.0 avoids compatibility issues with rasterio and geopandas which may not have updated yet.
- `pydantic>=2.5.0` — Pydantic v2 (Rust-powered) is 5-17× faster than v1. The `@field_validator` decorator syntax used here is v2-only.
- `pyogrio>=0.7.0` — GeoPandas 0.14+ uses `pyogrio` as the default I/O backend instead of `fiona`. `pyogrio` is ~10× faster for reading/writing vector files.

